From fe282c45eea2d7f7950806b42f27c377eaacf21e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:36:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ptm/fs/hid: handle calls seen with NetPass and Tomodachi Life

- ptm:sysm ConfigureNew3DSCPU (0x0818): NetPass calls it at start to
  switch the New 3DS 804 MHz clock and L2 cache. Accept it; the emulated
  CPU speed is an emulator setting.
- fs:USER ReadExtSaveDataIcon (0x0853): NetPass reads its SpotPass
  extdata icon. Return the icon Tangelo stores when the extdata is
  created (ExtSaveDataInfo in words 1-4, size, mapped output buffer;
  replies with the number of bytes written).
- ptm GetStepHistory: Tomodachi Life asks for 24 hours from midnight.
  Report the same virtual walk as GetTotalStepCount (patch 0009): each
  hour gets the steps the counter advanced in it, the current hour up
  to now, future hours none, so the history adds up to the total.
- hid GetGyroscopeLowCalibrateParam: returning the default calibration
  without a real console is intended; log it at debug instead of as a
  stub warning.

